2 CONT Kyrkoherde (Vicar) i Lekåsa
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Jonas Laurentii. Levde 1574 i Bitterna (R). Kyrkoherde 1607 i Lekåsa (R). Död 1620 i Lekåsa (R). Kyrkoherde.  Gift
2 CONT
2 CONT Jonas Laurentii. Död troligen omkring 1620. Kyrkoherde i Lekåsa.  Källa Stig Svensson, runeby@telia.com. 
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------------------
2 CONT Jonas Laurentii Lechander (ca. 1540 - ca. 1620,  Lekåsa parish, ~ 80 years) 
2 CONT By Gerd Johansson (2000)
2 CONT
2 CONT "The Lechander family is said to descend from Jonas Laurentii, vicar of Lekåsa from 1582 to 1603. It is a grandson of his who states that he is the ancestor. Where the name Lechander comes from is not so difficult to understand. J
2 CONC onas was present at the Uppsala meeting in 1593 and he signed the meeting's decision to abolish the 'Red Book'. This meant the end of [Swedish King] Johan III's Catholic-inspired liturgy [the rRed Book' (1576)] and the Reformation
2 CONC  had won. All of Jonas's five known sons became priests and his four daughters married priests. Of the sons, at least three were married to priests' daughters.
2 CONT
2 CONT "One of his sons (Nils) also became vicar of Lekåsa, as did Nils' son Abraham. Two of Abraham's sons became commissioners in Lekåsa. In this way, four generations of Lechander have been priests there. I have 34 known grandchildren
2 CONC  of Jonas Laurentii, 17 boys and 17 girls. Of the boys, 11 became priests and of the girls, 11 married priests. There are also many priests among the great-grandchildren. 20 boys were ordained by 44 known priests and of the 39 gir
2 CONC ls, 18 married priests. And the vast majority were active in Västergötland.
2 CONT
2 CONT "There may be an even higher proportion of priests among these, since some of their fates are unknown to me. Of course, there may also be more grandchildren and great-grandchildren than I know. Several of the boys also married pri
2 CONC ests' daughters. In the following generations, there are also many priests. Among them can be mentioned: Gothenburg Bishop Gustaf Björck d. 1888, Skara Bishop Sven Danell d. 1981 and the Västergötland revival priest Mårten Landahl
2 CONC  d. 1858.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Several members of the family seemed to have a fierce and violent temper. In 1681, the parish priest Jonas Lechander in Vedum (grandson) was reported to the domkapitlet [cathedral administration] in Skara after having assaulted a
2 CONC  regementspastor (regimental pastor) at a funeral (from the Vedum area).
2 CONT
2 CONT "His cousin Abraham Lechander, parish priest in Lekåsa, was accused several times in the consistory, among other things, of fighting and for having ordained a Christian woman with an ofrälse  (unsaved) man (the woman's brother pro
2 CONC tested).
2 CONT
2 CONT "Abraham managed to avoid dismissal on all occasions, but sometimes had to pay a fine. His son Nils had a difficult time. At first he had difficulty taking his priestly exam, then he was admonished to read his sermons more by hear
2 CONC t. In 1714 he had to hand over the parish ministership to his brother Johan because he had become blind the year before. He was to be allowed to keep his maintenance until his death, but lost this when he ordained a woman before s
2 CONC he was divorced from her former husband.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Abraham's brother Johannes also had problems. He suddenly left his post as commissar and lived for a few years elsewhere. There he was completely plundered during the Danish feud and was held captive for a few weeks. In 1676 he c
2 CONC ame to Larv as commissar. There the family with many small children first had to live on charity in a shed before they were given a place to live. There are more members of the family who distinguished themselves negatively, were 
2 CONC deposed, seemed to have suffered from mental illness, etc., but these will suffice.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Others fared better: for example Jonas Laurentii's son Lars Lechander who was promoted to magister   (master) in Vittenberg and eventually became domprost  (dean) in Skara and his brother's son Nils Lechander in Sunnersberg who b
2 CONC ecame kontraktsprost  (contract dean) and member of parliament. Nils died in 1726 ‘after he had presided over the Sunnersberg congregation for 42 years with excellent zeal and activity.’
2 CONT
2 CONT "It is believed that the name Lechander died out with the last male in direct descent in the middle of the 18th century. But whether this is true is uncertain because not all branches have been followed. Possibly one branch moved 
2 CONC to Finland. In any case, the family has spread throughout Västergötland through the family's daughters. 
2 CONT
2 CONT "Sources: 
2 CONT - Joh. W. Warholm 'Skara Stifts Herdaminne'  (1871) (a personal history of clergy), https://runeberg.org/skarahe1/
2 CONT - Hilding Johansson's books 'Vedumsbygden' (1954), 'Bitternabygden' (1978) and 'Barne-Åsaka då och nu' (1961) (then and now)
2 CONT - Alexander Gustavsson 'En Västgötsk prästsläkt ur Västgötajul' (1952)
2 CONT - Genealogist Ingemar Hagman (1935-), Jönköping
2 CONT
2 CONT "Edited by Gerd Johansson, with help from his sons, Jacob and Linus (2000)."
2 CONT https://family.brudvik.org/genealogy/getperson.php?personID=I790&tree=brudvik
2 CONT https://gw.geneanet.org/karosenius?lang=sv&n=lechander&p=jonas+laurentii
2 CONT -----------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT From "Skara stift herdaminne"  (1871), p. 449: "Jonas Laurentii became parish priest in Lekåsa parish in 1582 and signed the Upps[sala] meeting resolution in 1593. He is said to have died in 1596, but probably lived until about 16
2 CONC 20.
2 CONT "With his wife Sigrid, he became the ancestor of the Lechander family.(*)
2 CONT Children: Bengt, pastor in Bollebygd, aged over 40. Nils, pastor in Lekåsa. Lars, dean in Skara. Johan, pastor in Bitterna. Abraham, regem.-pastor. Beata, married to Laur. Svenonis, pastor in Otterstad. Margareta, married to Bryno
2 CONC lf, pastor in Hessleskog. A daughter, married to Andr. Petri, pastor in Hjerpås. Ingrid, married to Gunn. Nic. pastor in Gökhem.
2 CONT "(*) Thus his grandson gives the name of the dean N. Lechander in Sunnersberg. Bishop Rbyzelius, on the other hand, accepts the successor John Nicolai as the ancestor of the family."
2 CONT
2 CONT Allan Anderson notes:
2 CONT my mm mm mm mm mf f  also my mf mm mm mm mf f
2 CONT Jonas Laurentil, aka Jonas Lechander, was kyrkoherde (pastor) at Lekåsa 1582-1603.
2 CONT
2 CONT All five Jonas's well-known sons became priests and his four daughters married priests. Of the sons at least three wed priest daughters. One of his sons (Nils) became Vicar in Lekåsa, likewise Nils's son Abraham. Two of Abraham's 
2 CONC sons became komministrar (assistant vicar) in Lekåsa. In this way, four generations of Lechanders have been priests. There are 34 well-known grandchildren to Jonas Laurentii, 17 boys and 17 girls. Of the boys, 11 became priests, a
2 CONC nd of the girls, 11 wed with priests. Also, among the great-grandchildren, many priests exist: 20 boys were pråstvigdes (ordained priests) of 44 well-known great-grandsons, and among the 39 great-granddaughters, 18 wed with priest
2 CONC s. There can exist a still high proportion priests of these, since not all of the grandchildren and great-grandchildren are known. Several of the boys married priest's daughters. Among them can be mentioned: Göteborgs biskopen Gus
2 CONC taf Björck d. 1888, Skara biskopen Sven Danell d. 1981 and the Västgötska religious revival priest Mårten Landahl d. 1858.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jonas was present at the Uppsala meeting in 1593. This is where the Swedish Lutheran church formerly adopted the Augsburg Confession, after separating from the Roman Catholic Church.  A transcript of the "Confessio Fidei" (Confess
2 CONC ion of Faith) from the 1593 Uppsala Synod is at https://sv.wikisource.org/wiki/Uppsala_mötes_beslut_1593 Under "Kyrkioherdar på Landzbyghden j Westergöthland" signs "Ionas in Leekååsa."
2 CONT
2 CONT Residences: birth-death Lekåsa (R). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT Jonas Laurentii biography, from "Skara stift herdaminne"  (1871), p. 449, https://runeberg.org/skarahe1/0455.html
2 CONT Johan Wilhelm Warholm, "Skara stifts herdaminne (1871), p 441, mentions Jonas Laur. as father of Johannes Lechander, https://runeberg.org/skarahe1/0447.html
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------------------
