2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT From Sikeborg: Sheriff (länsman) in Skellefteå (Kråken). At Yttervik 2, Skellefteå about 1551.
2 CONT From Lundström (1997), quoted by Sikeborg: Lars Andersson appears 1551–1596 for the tax home (skattehemman) in Yttervik, which later received land registry number 2. He was a well-to-do man who traded in fish and leather goods. To
2 CONC gether with [Bureättlingen] Thomas Kättilsson [Kälsson] in Kåge, he owned a schooner on which the goods were transported for sale to Stockholm. "After Per Tomasson's death in 1552, he was in charge of the key to the church treasur
2 CONC y. He was sexton in 1552, 1554 and 1584–1585. Lars Andersson was a member of the council 1548–1584, a merchant 1549–1566 and a sheriff 1567–1569 and 1578." According to Lundström, Lars Andersson was the son of the previous farmer,
2 CONC  Anders Larsson, who is recorded in the farm 1543–1549, but it is not clear from the account if this relationship is explicitly stated in the sources or if it is an assumption . . ."
2 CONT
2 CONT "A letter which shows that the rich Sheriff (Länsman) Lars Andersson at Viken (now Yttervik), Skellefteå, married to Jacob Andersson's son's daughter Anna Mosesdotter sat on the committee in 1561 [p.146r]." (from familysearch LKBV
2 CONC -GHF note.)
2 CONT
