1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Recently another member updated this profile with the surname Anderson.  Anni used Thorsén .  Anderson is a surname adopted by two brothers, Anders   (Andrew),  Anni's husband, and Johan (John), when they immigrate
2 CONC d to Vermont. While in Sweden they used Andersson and Larsson. Out of respect for Anni, I have kept her profile as Thorsén.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Stora Kungsryd is the proper spelling. The county was Skaraborg until 1997.  Please do not edit this again. Thank you. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT I'm very curious why Anni chose to move to what is still a very rural area of Vermont.  I've learned from immigration records her last European residence seems to have been in Sjogerstad.  Anni departed from Göteborg, with a recor
2 CONC d date of 31 Maj, 1901. Her destination was Chester, Vermont.  At this time, the "Anderson" family was living nearby in Grafton, Vermont which was, and is, even more rural than Chester.  (For anyone not familiar, which will be mos
2 CONC t reading, Upper Bartonsville, where Anni and her family created a homstead is a tiny village between Chester and Grafton.  Even now, in the 2020s, you will find unpaved roads, to give you a feel for the surroundings.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Since my great grandparents married shortly after, I am assuming they may have known one another, or had some common connections in Sweden, but I have not discovered what those may have been.  The two branches of these families se
2 CONC em to have lived very different lives, and I am quite naturally curious. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Everything I have found while researching Anni indicates hers was a life of struggle, so I am leaving her a song of ancient magic. 
2 CONT
