1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1653
2 PLAC Gruvad, Laske-Vedum, Vara, Skaraborg, Suède
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 31 AUG 1708
2 PLAC Stupad i krig Miskowitz i Polen, Pologne
2 ADDR
1 OCCU Captain First Class, kapten
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Haggman (Lars) surname in Skaraborg Regiment 1695: https://sok.riksarkivet.se/bildvisning/A0028422_00304
2 CONT
2 CONT BJÖRCK and LECHANDER (spelling) http://runeberg.org/skarahe1/0573.html
2 CONT ---
2 CONT As global borders have changed, I entered death place as current-day Belarus, but it formerly was Poland's territory, and most genealogies still say Poland. I think it is important to retain knowledge of precise locations when we 
2 CONC can, especially in honorable deaths like Captain Bjork's. - DeniseG 2023
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------------
2 CONT [Deleted 24 redundant references to different MyHeritage trees naming Ingemar Björk]
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Captain Björk died in the war in Poland serving w/ Skaraborgs regemente (present day Belarus).
2 CONT Befäl in (Commanded in) Skaraborgs regemente (Source Aktnr: SK-BEFÄLET-1674).
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Excerpt from Swedish Biographical Dictoinary: "Ingemar Bengtsson, of Gruvara in Laske-Vedum parish, who entered military service in 1674 and adopted the family name Björck. Captain in the Skaraborg regiment in 1702, he fell in the
2 CONC  engagement at Miskowitz on 31 Aug. 1708. He was the great-grandfather of the mathematics lecturer in Gothenburg, titular professor Elias Daniel B. (b. 1775, d. 1827)."
2 CONT Befäl (Commanded) in Skaraborgs regemente (Source Aktnr: SK-BEFÄLET-1674).  Military service (from geneanet): non-commissioned officer at Skaraborgs reg. 1674; ensign there 1686 19/2; lieut. there 1700 30/4; sec.captain there 1702
2 CONC  20/10; prem. captain there 1703 4/11; killed 1708 31/8 at Meskowitz.
2 CONT Befäl (Commanded) in Skaraborgs regemente (Source Aktnr: SK-BEFÄLET-1674). Military service (from geneanet): non-commissioned officer at Skaraborgs reg. 1674; ensign there 1686 19/2; lieut. there 1700 30/4; sec.captain there 1702 
2 CONC 20/10; prem. captain there 1703 4/11; killed 1708 31/8 at Meskowitz.
2 CONT
2 CONT Captain Ingemar Björk and Beata Lechander are mentioned in their son Elias Björk's biography, in "Skara stifts herdaminne": "Mag. Elias Björk, son of the captain of Skarab. regem Ingemar B. [Björk](**) and Beata Lechander, b. in B
2 CONC itterna d. 23 March 1693 . . .
2 CONT (**) He died in the Polish war. One of his sons, and brother to Elias, was Johan Björk, prestv. 1717, died as adj. in Bitterna."
2 CONT
2 CONT His FamilySearch profile shows, without sources, that Bengt Ingemarsson and Anna Carlsdotter are his parents. His Geni profile shows, also without sources, that Hans Andersson Björk and Kristina are his parents. Who to believe? No
2 CONC body, until some source is found.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT Swedish Biographical Dictionary article on Björck family, https://sok.riksarkivet.se/sbl/Presentation.aspx?id=18272
2 CONT Son Elias biography in Johan Wilhelm Warholm, "Skara stifts herdaminne" (pastoral memory), (1871), p. 567-568, section 16, https://runeberg.org/skarahe1/0573.html
2 CONT https://gw.geneanet.org/idahl?lang=sv&p=ingemar&n=bjorck
2 CONT Account of battle where he died in 1708 at Malatitze is at http://www.skaraborgarna.se/historia/malatitze-1708/
2 CONT
2 CONT Familysearch profile, https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/details/LZDL-VB5
