1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT Draft card. attached notes Anders was of medium height & build with brown hair & eyes. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth surname was "Andersson".  Anderson is the Americanized spelling used by himself and his brother Johan, aka "John", when the moved to Vermont..  On at least one occasion, the draft in World War 1, he gave his middle name as "
2 CONC Gustavus". 
2 CONT
2 CONT Also be advised, he occasionally provides a slightly different birthdate of December 10th. I am certain this is the same person, as his parents, siblings, birthplace and addresses in Sweden match.  His church records in Sweden sho
2 CONC w his date of birth as December 8, 1875 and his baptism date as December 10, 1875.
2 CONT
2 CONT _________________________________________________________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT I was told members of the family went to Minnesota prior to Vermont.  I found an Andrew G. Anderson born in December of 1875 in the 1900 Census working as a laborer in Minnesota. If same person, he immigrated initially in 1894. Wi
2 CONC ll continue to research.  Karrie. ( note added July 26, 2022)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1900 United States Federal Census -''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT Andrew G Anderson
2 CONT State: MinnesotaCounty: CottonwoodTownship: Westbrook TownshipSheet: 7Family: 128Line: 79Image: 12
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Name	Andrew G Anderson
2 CONT Gender	Male
2 CONT Birth	Dec 1875
2 CONT   Sweden
2 CONT Residence	1900
2 CONT   Westbrook Township, Cottonwood, Minnesota, USA
2 CONT Age	25
2 CONT Marital status	Single
2 CONT Immigration	1894
2 CONT Race	White
2 CONT Ethnicity	American
2 CONT
2 CONT ********************
2 CONT This may not be the same person, as I do have records which I am 100% confident are my great grandfather coming to America from Sweden with one of his brothers in 1901. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Anders did spend at approximately one year in the United States as Swedish Census records show him leaving in 1895 and returning again in 1896. I cannot rule out the record above in Minnesota, as US Census records in my experience
2 CONC  often estimate.  Continuing to research. * Feb 25, 2024
